1
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:47,519
It's a bit big.

2
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:50,560
Boss, can this be altered?

3
00:01:52,439 --> 00:01:53,239
Can't be altered.

4
00:01:53,319 --> 00:01:54,599
People don't usually try these on themselves.

5
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,599
Could you take that yellow one up there

6
00:02:00,599 --> 00:02:01,439
down for me to try on?

7
00:02:01,439 --> 00:02:02,599
This is a shroud shop.

8
00:02:03,079 --> 00:02:04,359
We don't have that many styles.

9
00:02:04,359 --> 00:02:05,319
Just pick one.

10
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:06,200
Mind if I ask,

11
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,039
is it for a man or a woman?

12
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:09,280
How old were they when they passed?

13
00:02:09,439 --> 00:02:10,680
A man. In his forties.

14
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:11,479
Your brother passed away?

15
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:12,280
It's for myself.

16
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:14,599
Bro, with your complexion,

17
00:02:14,599 --> 00:02:16,280
I think it's a bit early to prepare.

18
00:02:16,319 --> 00:02:17,840
In my experience, you'll still lose weight.

19
00:02:17,879 --> 00:02:18,879
I just want something that has a...

20
00:02:18,879 --> 00:02:20,159
a more, you know, Western style.

21
00:02:20,159 --> 00:02:21,000
The kind with a tie.

22
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,840
Something that makes me look educated. Got any?

23
00:02:25,039 --> 00:02:27,479
Chinese style is the most cultured.

24
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:29,680
Plus, they won't accept Western styles down there.

25
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,360
Hello there.

26
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:39,080
I want to get new lenses for these glasses.

27
00:02:39,639 --> 00:02:40,520
What's your price range?

28
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,479
Give me the most expensive ones.

29
00:02:41,479 --> 00:02:42,400
Before I go, I want to see

30
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,599
this filthy world clearly.

31
00:02:43,719 --> 00:02:46,199
Zeiss HD. 5,700.

32
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,080
Is this filthy world worth 5,700?

33
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:51,879
A 200-yuan pair will do.

34
00:02:52,919 --> 00:02:54,120
Give me ten billion worth of these.

35
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:55,039
I can't sell half a bundle.

36
00:02:55,039 --> 00:02:56,159
If, if you really want it,

37
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:57,319
you can have a bundle for five bucks.

38
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,199
I can't break it open.

39
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,639
Well, if my budget is 500,

40
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:01,039
how much can I burn from here?

41
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,520
If you're ready to spend 500 bucks,

42
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,599
anything in this shop except me,

43
00:03:03,599 --> 00:03:04,560
you can burn whatever you want.

44
00:03:05,319 --> 00:03:06,199
Understood.

45
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:08,039
Are these all the words you want engraved?

46
00:03:08,199 --> 00:03:08,879
Just these.

47
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,039
Okay, it'll be done in three hours.

48
00:03:10,039 --> 00:03:11,000
Just wait a moment.

49
00:03:11,039 --> 00:03:11,800
Boss, can I leave my plastic bag

50
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:12,800
here for a bit?

51
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:13,599
I'm going to look around.

52
00:03:13,759 --> 00:03:14,560
No problem.

53
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:15,680
Thanks.

54
00:03:17,039 --> 00:03:17,759
How much is this house?

55
00:03:17,759 --> 00:03:18,680
50 bucks each.

56
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:19,680
Can you make it cheaper?

57
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,639
Do you know the market right now?

58
00:03:20,639 --> 00:03:21,400
Housing prices are so high!

59
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,400
Then throw in a car.

60
00:03:23,039 --> 00:03:24,039
A Rolls-Royce.

61
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:24,800
A driver,

62
00:03:25,199 --> 00:03:25,960
car keys,

63
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:27,240
and a driver's license are all included.

64
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:28,080
It's more expensive than the house.

65
00:03:29,639 --> 00:03:30,680
Tell you what, tell you what, Bro.

66
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,479
If you really want it,

67
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,439
I'll throw in a phone.

68
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,879
An iPhone 18 Pro Max.

69
00:03:36,879 --> 00:03:37,639
I'll throw it in for free.

70
00:03:39,919 --> 00:03:40,919
Does it come with a charging cable?

71
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,680
Here, buddy, what are you having?

72
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:44,680
I'll have it all.

73
00:03:45,159 --> 00:03:46,960
Two dishes are plenty for one person.

74
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:47,960
Our portions are huge.

75
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:49,319
I'll take both sides of the menu.

76
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,639
I don't want to be a hungry ghost.

77
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,199
Ma'am, can I cancel some of it?

78
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:03,639
Two dishes really is the limit for my stomach.

79
00:04:03,639 --> 00:04:04,560
The other half is

80
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,400
already cooking on the stove.

81
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,360
Weren't you acting so tough? Try them all.

82
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:29,000
A woman who doesn't want your house or car,

83
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,800
washes your feet, and gives you a massage.

84
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,680
And she only charges 129 for 60 minutes.

85
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:33,800
Is that expensive?

86
00:04:37,079 --> 00:04:37,800
Not at all.

87
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,319
Hello, sir.

88
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:48,560
Technician 38, at your service.

89
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,360
You can call me Xiaoyun.

90
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,199
We have a 129 package,

91
00:04:52,199 --> 00:04:53,120
a 229 package,

92
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,319
and a 399 package.

93
00:04:54,319 --> 00:04:55,279
Which one would you like?

94
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,480
We also have entertainment on the second floor.

95
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:05,839
Which way?

96
00:05:07,079 --> 00:05:07,639
This way, please.

97
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,199
Is this the special skill you mentioned?

98
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:23,920
The cultural heritage one?

99
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:33,800
Come here. Let me talk to you for a sec.

100
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:37,800
I still have 20,000 on my card.

101
00:05:38,879 --> 00:05:40,000
I can show you.

102
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:43,759
I'll give it all to you.

103
00:05:47,839 --> 00:05:49,319
Could you give me some warmth?

104
00:05:50,759 --> 00:05:52,879
Bro, we run a clean business here.

105
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,759
No, I didn't mean it like that.

106
00:05:54,879 --> 00:05:55,920
I just mean...

107
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:59,639
I haven't felt any warmth from this world.

108
00:05:59,639 --> 00:06:01,160
Could you give me some?

109
00:06:01,399 --> 00:06:03,079
Or even just a hug... I... I...

110
00:06:03,319 --> 00:06:05,480
Just... just let me experience...

111
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:06,600
what warmth feels like.

112
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:08,519
Okay, okay.

113
00:06:08,519 --> 00:06:09,560
Just a hug. Strictly a hug.

114
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:10,319
Got it, got it.

115
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:12,120
The door's unlocked. Give me a sec.

116
00:06:15,279 --> 00:06:16,480
Help! Security!

117
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,040
There's a pervert in 666!

118
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,600
Security! Help!

119
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:20,560
Security!

120
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,560
There's a pervert in 666! Security!

121
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:24,120
It's a misunderstanding! A misunderstanding!

122
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,360
What are you doing?

123
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:38,959
He ran off.

124
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:40,920
So fast.

125
00:06:42,959 --> 00:06:44,399
Is he okay jumping from that high?

126
00:06:46,439 --> 00:06:47,800
So shameless.

127
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:49,879
Dirty old man!

128
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,680
The way he looked,

129
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,720
he was quite pitiful too.

130
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,720
I figured a massage is just a massage.

131
00:06:57,319 --> 00:06:58,680
Who knew he'd pull out 20,000 yuan

132
00:06:58,680 --> 00:06:59,759
and demand to sleep with me.

133
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,040
That's just so shameless.

134
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,120
What... What does he take me for?

135
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:08,120
Thanks, Pig Brother, for the sports car!

136
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,160
Let me do a dance for you.

137
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,120
What did I say?

138
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,480
What did I say?

139
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,160
Didn't I say I just wanted you to

140
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,120
give me some warmth?

141
00:07:17,639 --> 00:07:19,120
I just wanted you to hold me.

142
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,360
When did I say I wanted to pay you for sex?

143
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,120
Even if you

144
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:23,879
gave me money, I wouldn't sleep with you!

145
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:31,160
My phone!

146
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:40,879
Boss?

147
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,519
What do you need?

148
00:07:42,959 --> 00:07:43,720
I want to take a picture.

149
00:07:44,639 --> 00:07:45,480
A picture? Sure.

150
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,480
What kind?

151
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,279
Just... Just one about that big.

152
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:51,720
Okay.

153
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,600
I want it black and white.

154
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:53,680
Black and white?

155
00:07:55,759 --> 00:07:56,639
Black and white.

156
00:07:58,639 --> 00:07:59,160
Bro,

157
00:07:59,399 --> 00:08:00,839
you're already here, so cheer up.

158
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,160
Come on, let's try it.

159
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,680
Come on, smile a little.

160
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:04,240
Cheer up. Come on.

161
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:05,399
Smile. Come on.

162
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,399
Good, good, good. Come on.

163
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,279
Looks great. Looks great.

164
00:08:09,279 --> 00:08:10,519
Looking sharp.

165
00:08:11,079 --> 00:08:12,279
Good. Good.

166
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,279
Isn't this a good thing?

167
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:16,040
Good, good, good.

168
00:08:20,079 --> 00:08:20,920
Pretty good.

169
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,199
Pretty good.

170
00:08:22,839 --> 00:08:23,519
How much?

171
00:08:24,439 --> 00:08:25,199
No charge.

172
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:36,360
WeChat payment received: 10,000 yuan

173
00:08:37,799 --> 00:08:38,960
That's too generous.

174
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:40,600
Auntie Sun,

175
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,200
thank you for taking care of me for so long.

176
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:44,960
I've owed you rent for so long.

177
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,120
I'm sorry.

178
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:47,279
Farewell.

179
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:49,639
I don't need the books in my room anymore.

180
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,000
Leave them for the kids to read.

181
00:08:52,919 --> 00:08:55,759
Alipay payment received: 10,000 yuan

182
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,600
This piece of junk won't sell for much.

183
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,559
At least give me something.

184
00:09:00,559 --> 00:09:01,840
It's no use to me anyway.

185
00:09:03,399 --> 00:09:04,080
It has no value.

186
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,399
This thing is worthless.

187
00:09:10,679 --> 00:09:12,159
It's time for class.

188
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:14,559
Students, please line up,

189
00:09:14,559 --> 00:09:16,200
enter the classroom quietly,

190
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:17,559
and get ready for class.

191
00:09:53,919 --> 00:09:54,720
Fang Haowen.

192
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,200
Fang Haowen.

193
00:10:02,799 --> 00:10:03,440
Stand up.

194
00:10:07,039 --> 00:10:08,159
Not wearing your uniform again.

195
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,440
Always trying to be special.

196
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,600
Come on, bring your essay up here.

197
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,440
Read it to the class.

198
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:13,480
So everyone can appreciate it.

199
00:10:29,159 --> 00:10:30,320
My father.

200
00:10:30,879 --> 00:10:32,639
My father is illiterate.

201
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,320
But he's still very happy.

202
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:36,240
What's happy about being illiterate?

203
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,639
Fang Haowen's dad is illiterate!

204
00:10:38,639 --> 00:10:41,080
Fang Haowen's dad is illiterate!

205
00:10:41,080 --> 00:10:43,519
Fang Haowen's dad is illiterate!

206
00:10:43,519 --> 00:10:44,639
Quiet! Quiet!

207
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:47,399
This is a classroom! Continue.

208
00:10:48,679 --> 00:10:50,679
His job is driving a cart.

209
00:10:50,679 --> 00:10:53,399
People respectfully call him Master Fang.

210
00:10:53,559 --> 00:10:55,159
He also always tells me

211
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:56,840
to study hard

212
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:58,120
and become educated.

213
00:10:58,200 --> 00:11:00,919
He said he did the "travel ten thousand miles" part for me.

214
00:11:00,919 --> 00:11:03,639
All I need to do is "read ten thousand books".

215
00:11:07,559 --> 00:11:09,200
I just read my essay out loud.

216
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,600
What do you think of it?

217
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,399
Not that great. There aren't any idioms.

218
00:11:12,559 --> 00:11:15,399
And I don't see any literary mystery.

219
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:16,600
It's mastery.

220
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,919
Mastery. Mastery.

221
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:21,480
Then I'll have to learn more idioms.

222
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,639
Here's your favorite chocolate.

223
00:11:24,799 --> 00:11:26,320
I had my dad bring it back.

224
00:11:26,919 --> 00:11:29,120
That's nice. You don't even like it, but you brought it for me.

225
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:30,120
Of course.

226
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,000
Hello, Mr. Xu.

227
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,480
Do you still remember me?

228
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:34,200
It's been at least ten years since we last saw each other.

229
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,559
I became principal ten years ago.

230
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:38,200
Call me Principal Xu.

231
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,159
Thirty years ago, I was your student.

232
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,759
See?

233
00:12:41,919 --> 00:12:43,200
Ten years is an understatement.

234
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,480
It's been thirty years.

235
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,679
You taught me. Did you forget?

236
00:12:47,879 --> 00:12:49,120
Back then, I read the essay you wrote

237
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:50,600
and won first place in the citywide

238
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,200
elementary school essay speech contest.

239
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,279
Did you?

240
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:56,919
You said I was the pride of the class.

241
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:59,000
Said I was the pride of the school.

242
00:12:59,159 --> 00:13:00,120
You also said that in the near future,

243
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:02,600
I might become a rising literary star.

244
00:13:05,799 --> 00:13:07,200
Wang Xuedong, right?

245
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:08,879
Fang Haowen.

246
00:13:09,799 --> 00:13:11,039
My dad is illiterate.

247
00:13:11,799 --> 00:13:12,679
I remember now.

248
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:14,720
Fang Haowen, Fang Haowen. Right.

249
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,080
Mr. Xu...

250
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:19,840
Call me Principal.

251
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,000
Mr. Xu, I hate you.

252
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:21,799
Call me Principal.

253
00:13:21,799 --> 00:13:22,679
I hate you, Principal.

254
00:13:23,679 --> 00:13:25,600
Wait, why do you hate the principal?

255
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:28,320
Because I'm not the pride of the class now.

256
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,840
Nor the pride of the school.

257
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:34,200
And I didn't become a rising literary star.

258
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:35,720
Then take it up with the literary world.

259
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,080
Why are you taking it up with the principal?

260
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,639
I shouldn't have listened to you back then.

261
00:13:38,799 --> 00:13:40,200
I shouldn't have read the essay you wrote.

262
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,440
I should have read the one I wrote myself.

263
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,320
"My Father."

264
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:46,360
And I shouldn't have listened to Jin Furong

265
00:13:47,120 --> 00:13:48,080
and written success guides.

266
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,919
I should have published my own poetry collection.

267
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,480
You even published a book?

268
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,279
I shouldn't have helped you back then.

269
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,320
If it weren't for your dad,

270
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,960
I wouldn't have bothered helping you.

271
00:13:58,960 --> 00:13:59,679
My dad?

272
00:14:07,639 --> 00:14:08,840
Just because I'm illiterate,

273
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:10,240
it's given the kid an inferiority complex.

274
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,200
This contest,

275
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,279
he talks about it at home every day.

276
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:13,320
Seems he really cares about it.

277
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:14,559
Please give him a chance.

278
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,600
The kid loves literature.

279
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:17,639
Loves reading.

280
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:19,200
He's read every book at home cover to cover.

281
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,480
Three Hundred Tang Poems,

282
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,720
he can recite it backwards.

283
00:14:21,720 --> 00:14:23,000
Comrade Fang Shuanniu,

284
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:26,279
I completely understand how you feel.

285
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:28,600
But this is an essay contest.

286
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:31,360
Contests must be fair and just.

287
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,080
If his essay is really good,

288
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,480
the school will definitely recommend it.

289
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:35,360
But with his current level...

290
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:36,320
Mr. Xu, listen to me.

291
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,679
The kid's had it rough.

292
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,679
His mom left before he was even weaned.

293
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,679
I'm always out driving and not at home.

294
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,879
When he was shorter than the stove,

295
00:14:49,879 --> 00:14:51,000
he was already cooking for himself.

296
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,600
If he could just enter this contest

297
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,679
and maybe win an award,

298
00:14:53,799 --> 00:14:55,000
wouldn't he gain some confidence?

299
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,480
Then he can hold his head high no matter what.

300
00:14:59,519 --> 00:15:00,200
Mr. Xu.

301
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,960
Mr. Xu, I'm begging you.

302
00:15:04,559 --> 00:15:05,720
Please help my kid.

303
00:15:05,799 --> 00:15:06,759
What are you doing?

304
00:15:06,759 --> 00:15:07,399
Get up!

305
00:15:07,399 --> 00:15:08,159
I'm begging you, Mr. Xu.

306
00:15:08,159 --> 00:15:08,840
Get up, quickly.

307
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:09,720
I'm begging you!

308
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:10,360
Come on.

309
00:15:13,159 --> 00:15:14,600
Please help my kid.

310
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:26,159
Do you think I wanted to do that back then?

311
00:15:27,799 --> 00:15:28,519
Fang Haowen.

312
00:15:28,919 --> 00:15:30,600
Your dad really kneeled on the ground,

313
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,320
crying his eyes out and begging me.

314
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:33,320
That's why I gave in.

315
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,159
Did you know that?

316
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:39,919
Fang Haowen,

317
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:44,840
Before you leave, two pieces of advice.

318
00:15:45,879 --> 00:15:46,480
First,

319
00:15:47,679 --> 00:15:50,000
Look for the cause within yourself first.

320
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,279
Second,

321
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,440
knock before you enter.

322
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:55,080
Learn to respect others.

323
00:15:55,759 --> 00:15:56,279
Now go.

324
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:15,360
Boss, do you have Dichlorvos?

325
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:16,759
Yes, yes, I do.

326
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,039
Here, twenty.

327
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:24,879
Is this stuff strong?

328
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:27,440
One small cap is enough for one mu.

329
00:16:28,919 --> 00:16:30,639
WeChat payment received: 200 yuan.

330
00:16:30,639 --> 00:16:31,600
Why did you pay 200?

331
00:16:32,879 --> 00:16:33,720
I'm not selling it. I'm not selling.

332
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:36,840
I'm not selling. Open your payment code.

333
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:37,480
I'll refund you. I'll refund you.

334
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:37,879
I'm not selling it! I'm not selling it!

335
00:16:37,879 --> 00:16:39,000
I paid extra, you have to give it to me.

336
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:39,799
I'll refund you! I'll refund you!

337
00:16:39,799 --> 00:16:41,000
Is this how you do business? I'll refund!

338
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,799
WeChat payment received: 100 yuan.

339
00:16:42,799 --> 00:16:43,159
It went through.

340
00:16:43,159 --> 00:16:44,039
This one is expired.

341
00:16:44,039 --> 00:16:44,799
I can't sell it to you.

342
00:16:44,799 --> 00:16:46,000
Let me get you another bottle.

343
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:46,679
No, just... just...

344
00:16:46,679 --> 00:16:47,360
Expired is fine.

345
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,600
It's stronger when expired. Give it to me.

346
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:49,600
No, no. I can't sell it to you.

347
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,679
But I already paid for it!

348
00:16:50,679 --> 00:16:51,679
Then... I'll refund you.

349
00:16:51,679 --> 00:16:52,360
I'll refund you. Just give it to me!

350
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:53,519
Give it to me! I paid!

351
00:16:53,519 --> 00:16:54,879
Tell you what, drink this.

352
00:16:55,159 --> 00:16:56,720
Let's cheer up a bit, okay?

353
00:16:56,799 --> 00:16:58,000
Just cheer up.

354
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:17,559
Are you going tomb sweeping or robbing?

355
00:17:23,599 --> 00:17:25,119
Boss, is it ready?

356
00:17:25,599 --> 00:17:26,880
The tombstone is ready. Are you alone?

357
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:28,359
You didn't drive?

358
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:29,039
No.

359
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:10,160
Dad,

360
00:18:10,359 --> 00:18:11,839
I haven't visited you in years.

361
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,640
Don't be mad at me.

362
00:18:19,920 --> 00:18:20,720
Dad.

363
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:23,720
I'm here to visit you now.

364
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:31,880
Excuse me.

365
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,519
Wait, was there a relocation or what?

366
00:18:42,079 --> 00:18:44,480
Dad, I haven't visited you in years.

367
00:18:45,680 --> 00:18:47,039
Don't hold it against me, Dad.

368
00:18:51,720 --> 00:18:52,359
Dad.

369
00:19:00,319 --> 00:19:02,400
For all these years,

370
00:19:04,079 --> 00:19:04,759
I've been busy.

371
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,359
Hustling alone in the big city.

372
00:19:10,359 --> 00:19:12,079
But I haven't made a name for myself.

373
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:15,359
You did the "travel ten thousand miles".

374
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,680
I did "read ten thousand books" as told.

375
00:19:20,079 --> 00:19:20,839
But it was totally useless.

376
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:24,079
I once harbored a heart full of ambitions,

377
00:19:24,319 --> 00:19:26,559
wanting to leave my mark on this world.

378
00:19:26,559 --> 00:19:27,319
But now,

379
00:19:31,319 --> 00:19:32,799
fame and fortune are just illusions.

380
00:19:32,799 --> 00:19:33,559
No one appreciates me.

381
00:19:36,039 --> 00:19:36,799
This world,

382
00:19:38,319 --> 00:19:39,000
I'm tired of it.

383
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:40,960
And I'm sick of it.

384
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,319
Right, Dad,

385
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,559
I wrote a new book.

386
00:19:48,559 --> 00:19:49,359
You haven't read it yet.

387
00:19:54,559 --> 00:19:55,799
I'll burn a copy for you later.

388
00:19:56,079 --> 00:19:58,440
Give it a read. I think it's pretty good.

389
00:20:00,799 --> 00:20:02,359
There's a poem in it dedicated to you.

390
00:20:04,319 --> 00:20:05,160
Let me read it to you.

391
00:20:06,599 --> 00:20:10,839
Poem: Silent Mourning, by Fang Haowen,

392
00:20:11,279 --> 00:20:13,759
also known as The Solitary Chanter.

393
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,000
During silent mourning,

394
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:19,200
bow your head as low as you can.

395
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:23,359
If tears should fall,

396
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:25,720
then,

397
00:20:26,799 --> 00:20:27,799
you, just like me,

398
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:29,759
have seen your own feet,

399
00:20:30,079 --> 00:20:31,440
and where they are heading.

400
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:33,880
What do you think?

401
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:36,559
True, this poem,

402
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:39,240
even though it isn't very long,

403
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:42,559
captures all facets of life in its lines.

404
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:45,200
Why am I even telling you this?

405
00:20:50,119 --> 00:20:50,759
Wait a minute,

406
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:52,519
we'll talk when we meet.

407
00:20:55,839 --> 00:20:58,480
Dad, here's the specific arrangement.

408
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,240
As for these 20 billion,

409
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,240
we'll split it half and half.

410
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:01,119
I asked around,

411
00:21:01,279 --> 00:21:01,920
down there,

412
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:03,039
it should last a while.

413
00:21:03,039 --> 00:21:04,000
We might not even finish it.

414
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,480
We might be reborn before we run out.

415
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,599
And this is a detached villa.

416
00:21:07,599 --> 00:21:08,960
You live upstairs, I'll live downstairs.

417
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:09,960
We won't bother each other.

418
00:21:10,119 --> 00:21:11,200
Look, there are even two staircases.

419
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:12,279
Whichever way you want to go,

420
00:21:12,279 --> 00:21:13,519
I'll... I'll just take the other one.

421
00:21:13,559 --> 00:21:15,519
Since you drove a big truck all your life,

422
00:21:15,519 --> 00:21:17,680
I got you a luxury car.

423
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:18,359
Rolls-Royce.

424
00:21:18,359 --> 00:21:18,960
Experience it for yourself.

425
00:21:20,039 --> 00:21:21,200
It should be pretty comfortable.

426
00:21:22,119 --> 00:21:22,839
Right, and this.

427
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:25,319
This iPhone 18 is mine.

428
00:21:25,319 --> 00:21:26,119
Keep it for me for now.

429
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:26,880
After I go down there,

430
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:28,680
I'll get you a senior phone.

431
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:31,559
All right, that's roughly the situation.

432
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:35,559
I'll send the money over to you first.

433
00:21:44,839 --> 00:21:45,960
That's why I brought a backup.

434
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,480
Ever seen someone with two backups, Dad?

435
00:21:57,799 --> 00:21:58,759
Am I a good son or what?

436
00:22:01,359 --> 00:22:02,119
Dad, do you...

437
00:22:02,119 --> 00:22:03,799
Do you have objections or what?

438
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,559
Not enough money, or the car isn't good?

439
00:22:05,559 --> 00:22:06,880
Or the house isn't good? What is it?

440
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,720
Wait until we meet, I'll tell you then.

441
00:22:11,720 --> 00:22:13,559
I'll explain this to you, okay?

442
00:22:14,079 --> 00:22:15,839
Such a mischievous old man, seriously.

443
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:17,640
Three lighters,

444
00:22:20,079 --> 00:22:20,960
and not a single one works.

445
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:35,880
I was here.

446
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:37,200
I loved.

447
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:38,680
I never plagiarized.

448
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,119
Exactly.

449
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,359
Give us a little intro

450
00:23:42,279 --> 00:23:43,000
Farewell,

451
00:23:46,279 --> 00:23:48,240
to this filthy world.

452
00:23:55,119 --> 00:23:55,880
I... my...

453
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:58,000
To answer President Jin,

454
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:59,279
President Jin is right!

455
00:23:59,640 --> 00:24:00,880
Fang Haowen, think this through.

456
00:24:01,039 --> 00:24:03,160
I gave you everything you have today.

457
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,519
You want to publish this book?

458
00:24:04,519 --> 00:24:05,640
It'll cost two, three hundred grand.

459
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:06,880
How about you front the money for me?

460
00:24:10,279 --> 00:24:11,839
Me, fronting the money for your book?

461
00:24:11,839 --> 00:24:14,119
Okay, okay. Mr. Fang. Mr. Fang.

462
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:15,720
The books are returned, it's fine.

463
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:16,680
Come on, drop the link.

464
00:24:16,680 --> 00:24:17,440
Can you hit me again?

465
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:18,160
I didn't do my hair.

466
00:24:18,160 --> 00:24:19,279
Wanna hit me, huh?

467
00:24:19,440 --> 00:24:20,960
Come on, hit me right here.

468
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,000
I'm judging by your face.

469
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:23,240
You're ugly and you're an awful person.

470
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:24,720
And your writing sucks too. Trash.

471
00:25:06,079 --> 00:25:07,680
You scammer selling fakes!

472
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:08,559
You'd even scam the dead!

473
00:26:10,200 --> 00:26:11,599
Just got these glasses.

474
00:27:13,599 --> 00:27:14,799
Mr. Fang!

475
00:27:18,519 --> 00:27:19,759
Mr. Fang!

476
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,000
Don't jump!

477
00:27:25,599 --> 00:27:28,480
Mr. Fang, you can't die!

478
00:27:30,079 --> 00:27:31,640
Mr. Fang, you can't die!

479
00:27:32,119 --> 00:27:32,839
Mr. Fang!

480
00:27:33,319 --> 00:27:34,559
I won't let you die!

481
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:35,440
I'm choking!

482
00:27:36,599 --> 00:27:37,160
Let go!

483
00:27:38,559 --> 00:27:39,839
Mr. Fang, get down!

484
00:27:47,079 --> 00:27:47,720
Right here.

485
00:27:48,519 --> 00:27:49,319
Let's make this quick.
